/-!
# Coherence of the structure sheaf of a locally ringed space, from local relations

Coherence of a sheaf of modules is defined by a condition on every object of the site and on
every one of its slice sites, which makes it awkward to transport between a space and its open
subspaces. This file provides a concrete replacement:
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.HasLocalRelations` says that, near every point, the
relations between finitely many sections of `𝒪_Y` are generated by finitely many of them. It
mentions only open subsets, sections and restriction maps, so it is manifestly local, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.isCoherentStructureSheaf_of_hasLocalRelations` shows it
implies coherence.

**There is nothing complex-analytic here, and there are now two consumers that prove it.** The
theorem is quoted for `ℂ^ι` in `Other/Oka/AnalyticSpace/Relations.lean`, where Oka's coherence lemma
supplies the hypothesis, and for a locally noetherian scheme in
`Other/Oka/AlgebraicGeometry/Modules/Coherent.lean`, where noetherianity does. See `README.md` on the
mirror tree.

## Where this would go upstream

A new file `Mathlib/Geometry/RingedSpace/LocallyRingedSpace/Coherent.lean`. Being new it costs no
existing Mathlib file anything; the Mathlib part of its transitive closure is **1861** modules,
which is 9 more than `Other/Oka/Geometry/RingedSpace/LocallyRingedSpace/Modules.lean`'s 1852; the
coherence machinery it adds on top of that file is almost entirely this repository's own.

**And that is the actual obstruction. At `v4.32.0`; the revision `lakefile.toml` pins, resolved
by `lake-manifest.json` to `81a5d257c8e410db227a6665ed08f64fea08e997`;
`SheafOfModules.IsCoherent` is not in Mathlib**: `grep -rn "SheafOfModules.IsCoherent" Mathlib/`,
run over `.lake/packages/mathlib` at that rev, returns **0** occurrences in **0** files, and over
the environment of `import Mathlib` at that rev the constant does not exist. It is
`Other/Oka/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/Coherent/Basic.lean`, itself a mirror file for a Mathlib
file that does not exist, and this file's `Oka` imports are that subtree plus
`Other/Oka/CategoryTheory/Sites/CoversTop/Over.lean` and
`Other/Oka/Geometry/RingedSpace/LocallyRingedSpace/Modules.lean`. So the mirror path is a claim about
where this belongs and not a claim that it could be upstreamed tomorrow: the coherence API has to
go first.

**Two readings, and the cheap instrument decides only the narrower one.** As a claim about the
**name** the `grep` decides outright, which is the verdict the three questions put to a scan offered
in support of an absence exist to reach: a consumer that wants `SheafOfModules.IsCoherent` has to
write that token in its own statement, whatever namespace is open; a `variable` binder introducing
a sheaf of modules leaves the predicate still to be written; and a `class` is declared and not
generated, so there is no elaborator-produced spelling for a scan of source to miss.

**The claim this paragraph needs is the wider one; that Mathlib has no coherence predicate for
sheaves of modules under *any* name; and no scan keyed on a name can decide that.** What decides it
is keyed on the **type**: a predicate on sheaves of modules is a declaration whose type is a
telescope of binders ending in `Prop` and mentioning the constant `SheafOfModules`, whatever the
declaration is called and whatever namespace it sits in. Over the environment of `import Mathlib` at
the rev above, **460** non-internal declarations have a type mentioning `SheafOfModules`, and
exactly **nine** of them are of that shape, all nine in that namespace:
`SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent`, `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`,
`SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation`, `SheafOfModules.Presentation.IsFinite`,
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.IsFiniteType`,
`SheafOfModules.QuasicoherentData.IsFinitePresentation`,
`SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData.IsFiniteType`, and; two names the environment of `import Other.Oka`
does not reach, so written with their namespace separate; `SheafOfModules`'s `IsLocallyFree` and
`SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData`'s `IsLocallyFreeData`. **Not one of them is coherence**, and
**seven of the nine write no form of the word at all**, the two nearest among them:
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` is
coherence's first half, and `SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation` asks for one local presentation
where coherence asks that the kernel of *every* map from a finite free sheaf be of finite type.

**Which telescope is a parameter of that scan, and the nine above are
`Lean.Meta.forallTelescope`'s.** `Lean.Meta.forallTelescopeReducing` unfolds before it stops, and
over the same environment it returns **eleven**: it adds `SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent` and
`SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentation`, lower-case `abbrev`s whose type ends in
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty (SheafOfModules R)`, which is `SheafOfModules R → Prop`. Each
carries `@[inherit_doc]` naming a class that is already among the nine;
`SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent` and `SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation` respectively; **so
what the reducing reading adds is a second exposure of a predicate the nine already hold, and not
one they missed**. The verdict is therefore invariant under the choice where the enumeration is
not: of the eleven, three write a form of *coherent* and eight write none, against two and seven
of the nine, and still not one of the eleven is coherence. The list above is the non-reducing
reading's and is left as it stands, the extra two being named here rather than folded into a list
that would then mean two things at once. The filter is `Lean.Name.isInternalDetail`
under both readings, and both telescopes are run on the whole type rather than on its head, which
is the only way a type ending in `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty` is reached at all. This
repository already names the parameter at another type-keyed scan:
`Other/Oka/AnalyticSpace/PullbackGlue.lean` takes the head of a codomain under
`Lean.Meta.forallTelescopeReducing` and says so where it states the scan, which is what the clause
above brings here.

**A positive control for coherence specifically, which the environment of `import Mathlib` cannot
supply, the verdict above being that there is nothing there to find.** The one coherence predicate
for sheaves of modules within this repository's reach is exposed in the same doubled way, and the
scan does see it: beside the class `SheafOfModules.IsCoherent` sits the `abbrev`
`SheafOfModules.isCoherent`, which packages it as a `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty`. Over the
environment of `import Other.Oka`; a different environment from the `import Mathlib` one every other
figure in this section is taken in; the same scan returns **634** declarations mentioning
`SheafOfModules`, **ten** of them Prop-valued under `forallTelescope` and **fourteen** under
`forallTelescopeReducing`. The ten are the nine above, less `SheafOfModules`'s `IsLocallyFree` and
`SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData`'s `IsLocallyFreeData`, which that environment does not reach,
plus this repository's `SheafOfModules.HasFiniteTypeRelations`, `SheafOfModules.IsCoherent` and
`SheafOfModules.LocallyGeneratesKernel`; the four the reducing reading adds are the two Mathlib
ones named above and this repository's `SheafOfModules.isCoherent` and
`SheafOfModules.isFiniteType`. **The class is among the ten and the `abbrev` is not**, so the
non-reducing walk is not blind to coherence; it holds `SheafOfModules.IsCoherent`; and what it
cannot see is a `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty` exposure standing alone. **That is the exact width
of the gap, and it is narrower than it looks**: all four such exposures across the two environments
stand beside a class the non-reducing walk already holds, so a Mathlib coherence predicate would
have had to carry no class at all to escape the nine above. That is a statement about the
instrument and about these two trees, and it leaves the verdict of this section, which the `import
Mathlib` runs decide, exactly where it was.

**The name-keyed run agrees with that verdict, and it is here as the narrowing run rather than the
deciding one; but it has to be asked in both spellings.** Of the **228** non-internal declarations
of that environment whose name writes some form of *coherent* in **any** case, **five** are
Prop-valued; `Topology.IsCoherentWith`, `CompactlyCoherentSpace`, `CategoryTheory`'s `Precoherent`
(a name `import Other.Oka` does not reach either, so written the same way),
`SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent` and `SheafOfModules.QuasicoherentData.IsFinitePresentation`; and
only the last two have a type mentioning a sheaf of modules at all, both of them
**quasi**-coherence, which is a different predicate and not the one this file's theorem needs. **The
case is the trap.** Inside the namespace `SheafOfModules`, which carries **430** non-internal
declarations, **seven** names write `Coherent` with a capital `C`;
`SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData`'s `quasiCoherentData` and its projections; where **66** write
some form of *coherent* in any case, because Mathlib spells it both ways in that one namespace:
camel `quasiCoherentData` beside lowercase `SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent` and
`SheafOfModules.QuasicoherentData`. A reader who runs the case-sensitive scan sees 7 of those 66,
which is the second reason the deciding instrument above is keyed on the type.

**Two residues, named rather than left for the next reader to find.** The predicate could have
been stated for Mathlib's *presheaves* of modules and transported: of the declarations whose type
ends in `Prop` and mentions `PresheafOfModules` there are exactly **two**,
`PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective` and `PresheafOfModules.IsLocallyInjective`, and neither is
coherence. Or it could have been stated for a sheaf valued in `ModuleCat` without naming
`SheafOfModules` at all: the same scan, asking for a type mentioning both `CategoryTheory.Sheaf`
and `ModuleCat`, returns **0**.

**The control is what stops the next reader running the shorter command and concluding this is
wrong.** `grep -rn "IsCoherent" Mathlib/` returns **28** occurrences in **8** files and not one
of them is about sheaves: **27** write `Topology.IsCoherentWith`, the structure declared at
`Mathlib/Topology/Defs/Induced.lean:125` whose lemmas are in `Mathlib/Topology/Coherent.lean`,
and the twenty-eighth is a `TODO` comment at
`Mathlib/Topology/Compactness/CompactlyCoherentSpace.lean:123` naming the bare token. **So the
bare token is not absent and the qualified name is**, and reporting the first run as a verdict
about the second would have been false. Every `grep` in this section is run over
`.lake/packages/mathlib` at the rev above and not over this tree, and every scan of the
environment over `import Mathlib` at that same rev.

**That clause read *`SheafOfModules.IsCoherent` is not in Mathlib* until 2026-09-21**, with no
version, no instrument and no control beside it;
`git show c6bfc1f:Other/Oka/Geometry/RingedSpace/LocallyRingedSpace/Coherent.lean` carries the retired
wording at `:36`, where it was the second half of the bolded lead. **The claim is unchanged and
only its warrant is.**

## What is *not* here, and where it went instead

The section and germ API this argument runs on; `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.res` and
its lemmas, the `imOpen`/`preOpen` pair for open subspaces, and the local-lifting lemmas
`exists_localCombination`, `exists_localLift` and `exists_localLift_family`; is in
`Other/Oka/Geometry/RingedSpace/LocallyRingedSpace.lean`, whose target is an **existing** Mathlib file
that all of it costs **nothing**. It was measured to compile against that file's own two imports
and no others, which is why it is there rather than here: a proposed file is a weaker claim than
an existing one, and none of that API mentions coherence.

## Main definitions

- `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.IsCoherentStructureSheaf`: `𝒪_Y` is coherent as a sheaf
  of modules over itself.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.HasLocalRelations`: the concrete relations condition, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.HasLocalRelationsOn` its relativisation to an open set,
  which is what an open cover argument quantifies over.

## Main results

- `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.isCoherentStructureSheaf_of_hasLocalRelations`: **local
  relations imply coherence.**
- `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.hasLocalRelations_of_openCover`: the condition may be
  checked on an open cover, and `AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyRingedSpace.HasLocalRelations.restrict`
  is the converse direction, that it passes to an open subspace.

## Provenance

Split out of `Other/Oka/AnalyticSpace/Relations.lean` for taxis #905, unchanged: no statement, proof or
name here differs from what that file held, and the split is by destination; the module theory
went to `Other/Oka/Geometry/RingedSpace/LocallyRingedSpace/Modules.lean`, the section and germ API to
`Other/Oka/Geometry/RingedSpace/LocallyRingedSpace.lean`, and what stayed behind is the three lines
about `ℂ^ι`.
